content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Conference Organizer",
      "description": "person responsible for planning and coordinating the overall conference"
    },
    {
      "name": "Conference",
      "description": "the full event that includes theme, agenda, and program",
      "attributes": [
        "Theme",
        "Agenda",
        "Conference Program"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Theme",
      "description": "central topic that defines the conference focus"
    },
    {
      "name": "Agenda",
      "description": "planned schedule of sessions and activities"
    },
    {
      "name": "Conference Program",
      "description": "collection of sessions and events included in the conference",
      "attributes": [
        "Session",
        "Networking Event"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Venue Booking",
      "description": "arrangement securing the physical location for the conference"
    },
    {
      "name": "Catering",
      "description": "coordination of food and beverage services for the event"
    },
    {
      "name": "Speaker",
      "description": "person presenting content or expertise at a session"
    },
    {
      "name": "Attendee",
      "description": "participant registered to join the conference"
    },
    {
      "name": "Feedback",
      "description": "attendee input on sessions or overall conference quality"
    },
    {
      "name": "Session Moderator",
      "description": "person leading the session flow and managing audience interaction"
    },
    {
      "name": "Session",
      "description": "individual event block featuring a speaker and presentation",
      "attributes": [
        "Presentation",
        "Audience Question"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Audience Question",
      "description": "question submitted by attendees during a session"
    },
    {
      "name": "Presentation",
      "description": "speaker delivered talk or visual material",
      "attributes": [
        "Session Material"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Session Material",
      "description": "supporting files or documents submitted by speakers"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sponsor",
      "description": "organization supporting the conference for visibility and networking"
    },
    {
      "name": "Branding Negotiation",
      "description": "discussion between organizer and sponsor about promotional opportunities"
    },
    {
      "name": "Networking Event",
      "description": "interactive gathering for attendees and sponsors to connect"
    },
    {
      "name": "Registration",
      "description": "attendee sign up process for conference participation"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reminder",
      "description": "notification sent to attendees regarding upcoming conference details"
    },
    {
      "name": "Accommodation Information",
      "description": "details provided to help attendees arrange lodging for the event"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Sponsoring": {
      "objects": [
        "Sponsor",
        "Branding Negotiation",
        "Networking Event"
      ]
    },
    "Attendance": {
      "objects": [
        "Attendee",
        "Conference Coordinator",
        "Registration",
        "Reminder",
        "Accommodation Information",
        "Feedback"
      ]
    },
    "Session Holding": {
      "objects": [
        "Session Moderator",
        "Speaker",
        "Session",
        "Audience Question",
        "Presentation",
        "Session Material"
      ]
    },
    "Organization": {
      "objects": [
        "Conference Organizer",
        "Conference",
        "Theme",
        "Conference Program",
        "Networking Event",
        "Session",
        "Catering",
        "Venue Booking"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- In case an object appears in multiple bounded contexts, suggest a name change.
- Also suggest a name change if the meaning of the object is too similar to an object from another bounded context
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
